  "description": "Proof-carrying collections for .NET. NonEmptyList<T> is a list the type system guarantees has at least one element, with collection expressions, list patterns, type-preserving LINQ, generic math, query-string binding, error-accumulating Validation, constraint types (AtLeast, Distinct, Sorted), NonEmptySet, NonEmptyDictionary, NonEmptyString, zipper, event stream, rose tree, non-empty async batching, and a bundled Roslyn analyzer and source generator.",
